{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>For [your ruins].</b> In place of 'your ruins,' and like it האתן בכורי פשעי [Micah 6:7] (shall I give the firstborn of my transgression), and ונשלמה פרים שפתינו (Hosea 14:3) (and let us pay the offering of our lips), or: for until now they were so." "<b>You are constrained from dwelling.</b> Because of the multitude of those who dwell, and they are all your children; therefore (the accent) and those who devoured you shall be far away."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {0 "Resolved ambiguous word האתן as 'shall I give' from Micah 6:7; the form can also be read as a plural noun ('the females'), but the parallel with the Hosea quotation supports the verbal reading."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:48.898622729Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}